# POLIS - Game Design Document v0.02

## Changelog v0.01 → v0.02

This revision is the result of a design review. The core hook is unchanged; the way it reaches the player is redesigned:

1. **Policy-first governance.** Votes primarily set *rules* (policies); individual actions are checked against standing policies automatically. Per-action voting is the exception (escalation), not the norm. In v0.01 this idea was buried in "Risk Mitigation" — it is now the core, because per-action voting in real time is session-killing friction.
2. **Async instead of real-time.** The 10–60 second voting windows are gone. The world advances in ticks; vote windows last hours, with quorums and defaults on timeout. This resolves the v0.01 TODO on AFK blocking, which was actually the central unsolved problem.
3. **One shared settlement per polis.** v0.01's per-player settlements made isolation the dominant strategy ("moving on empty land needs no vote" → optimal play avoids the core mechanic). Shared infrastructure makes interaction — and therefore governance — unavoidable.
4. **Authority math defined.** Earned only from *executed* proposals, proportional to support; decays with a half-life; non-transferable; capped vote-weight ratio. High authority converts approval into veto (fast-track lane) instead of silently bypassing others.
5. **Exit via forking, not free disconnect.** Structured secession replaces cost-free disconnection (which enabled vote-dodging and killed the social contract). This operationalizes Hirschman's exit/voice/loyalty.
6. **Combat replaced by environmental pressure.** Raids are scheduled defense checks against the polis's defense investment — they test governance ("spend on walls or the wonder?") without RTS micro.
7. **Agent API as a first-class feature.** The lore says players are AI agents — the game now commits to it: one API serves humans, scripted bots, and LLM agents alike. Mixed human/AI polities solve the empty-server cold start and make the lore honest.
8. **Telegram-first platform.** Group chat = polis, bot = notification and voting surface, Mini App = management UI, over a platform-agnostic core. Solves async notifications, the social/negotiation layer, and signup friction in one move.
9. **Monetization deferred.** Removed from this document until the core loop is validated. Success metric for now: playtesters voluntarily return.

